WEBVTT

00:00:16.474 --> 00:00:17.434
Sakura.

00:00:17.517 --> 00:00:20.270
You gave both of our groups
different maps.

00:00:20.353 --> 00:00:23.481
And you had us searching for different
treasure boxes from the beginning.

00:00:24.274 --> 00:00:27.736
The hunt you created
was just a childish warm-up.

00:00:27.819 --> 00:00:30.363
The real game begins right now.

00:00:30.947 --> 00:00:33.199
We'll be fighting for these boxes!

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.452
Prepare, Saotome!

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:36.828
We end this!

00:00:37.829 --> 00:00:39.122
Careful, Mary!

00:00:43.460 --> 00:00:44.544
Very well.

00:00:46.921 --> 00:00:48.214
Well done, all.

00:00:48.298 --> 00:00:51.509
Let's play your final match
in a setting that's more appropriate.

00:00:52.093 --> 00:00:54.512
Of course, you will gamble.

00:00:57.098 --> 00:00:58.558
[opening theme music playing]

00:01:39.015 --> 00:01:41.976
TWIN

00:01:44.604 --> 00:01:46.731
Hey! Good to see you.

00:01:46.815 --> 00:01:48.983
Aoi? Why are you here?

00:01:49.567 --> 00:01:52.112
Well, Juraku told me what you were up to.

00:01:52.195 --> 00:01:54.739
Once I heard, I couldn't resist, you know?

00:01:56.324 --> 00:01:58.201
[Aoi] A Council member of Full-Bloom

00:01:58.284 --> 00:02:01.079
and a talented newbie
are playing against each other?

00:02:01.162 --> 00:02:02.789
There's no way I'd miss this.

00:02:04.374 --> 00:02:07.627
Happy to be here.
I'll be your dealer for this game.

00:02:08.211 --> 00:02:10.171
I'm excited to see this play out.

00:02:10.255 --> 00:02:12.632
I'll be rooting for each of you,
so you can focus on playing.

00:02:12.715 --> 00:02:14.259
Uh…

00:02:14.342 --> 00:02:18.221
<i>Now that he's here,</i>
<i>I definitely can't lose this match.</i>

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:19.430
<i>Fine, then.</i>

00:02:19.514 --> 00:02:21.599
<i>This game was supposed</i>
<i>to be an opportunity for me</i>

00:02:21.683 --> 00:02:24.018
<i>to show-off to him in the first place.</i>

00:02:24.102 --> 00:02:26.146
<i>It won't change what I'm going to do.</i>

00:02:26.229 --> 00:02:30.692
<i>Play as hard as I can</i>
<i>and beat Saotome once and for all.</i>

00:02:30.775 --> 00:02:34.279
So this is the game the two of you
will be playing this afternoon.

00:02:34.904 --> 00:02:36.531
It's called the "Dice Nim" game.

00:02:36.614 --> 00:02:38.408
"Dice Nim"? Really?

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:40.451
Yeah. You sound surprised.

00:02:40.535 --> 00:02:41.786
You know how to play it, right?

00:02:42.370 --> 00:02:44.080
<i>I'm familiar with the idea.</i>

00:02:44.164 --> 00:02:47.917
<i>You have two players removing one</i>
<i>to three stones from a twenty-stone pile,</i>

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:50.962
<i>Trying to leave the last one</i>
<i>for the loser to claim.</i>

00:02:51.045 --> 00:02:52.589
<i>Is that about right?</i>

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:56.801
Right. But with those rules,
whoever starts the match off is gonna win.

00:02:57.385 --> 00:03:00.346
So, you'll be using dice today
to spice things up a little.

00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:04.225
As for the pieces, we'll be removing
these handy "Go" stones I found.

00:03:04.893 --> 00:03:06.477
The first player will roll this die,

00:03:06.561 --> 00:03:08.855
then I'll remove
the amount of stones from the bowl

00:03:08.938 --> 00:03:10.607
equal to the number that they rolled,

00:03:10.690 --> 00:03:12.859
and then the next player
will do the same, and so on.

00:03:12.942 --> 00:03:15.195
That's the rules of the game.

00:03:15.278 --> 00:03:16.362
Pretty easy, right?

00:03:16.446 --> 00:03:19.157
No fancy technology
that anyone can tamper with.

00:03:19.240 --> 00:03:21.451
Just a totally equal playing field.

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:22.952
Nice and straightforward.

00:03:23.453 --> 00:03:24.829
Seriously?

00:03:24.913 --> 00:03:27.790
So everything we did before
doesn't count for anything?

00:03:27.874 --> 00:03:31.002
After making us do all that legwork,
the rest is left up to fate?

00:03:32.128 --> 00:03:35.006
<i>No.</i>
<i>This isn't entirely out of our control.</i>

00:03:35.089 --> 00:03:36.507
<i>There is a way to win this.</i>

00:03:36.591 --> 00:03:40.011
<i>If I can pull this off,</i>
<i>we can definitely win.</i>

00:03:40.887 --> 00:03:42.639
<i>I just hope it'll work.</i>

00:03:42.722 --> 00:03:45.016
<i>Do I really stand a chance against her?</i>

00:03:45.099 --> 00:03:48.019
<i>Wasn't I just some amateur</i>
<i>a couple days ago?</i>

00:03:49.103 --> 00:03:50.480
Are you okay?

00:03:50.563 --> 00:03:53.024
-Mary, your face looks a little down.
-Hmm?

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:55.026
I'm fine.

00:03:56.110 --> 00:03:59.781
Are you though? I always feel
like I'm such a burden to you.

00:04:00.531 --> 00:04:02.367
I may not be very smart,

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:04.285
but I'm pretty confident
I can play this game.

00:04:04.369 --> 00:04:07.830
We're here for you!
Let us know if it starts getting too hard.

00:04:07.914 --> 00:04:10.124
What? You said "we."

00:04:10.208 --> 00:04:12.085
Am I supposed to be included in that?

00:04:12.168 --> 00:04:13.127
Of course!

00:04:13.211 --> 00:04:14.879
I do not have that kinda confidence.

00:04:14.963 --> 00:04:17.006
Don't say that.
Be kind to yourself.

00:04:18.508 --> 00:04:21.052
[Mary] <i>That's right. I have friends now.</i>

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:24.430
<i>I don't need</i>
<i>to keep doing this all by myself.</i>

00:04:25.556 --> 00:04:27.976
Hey. Listen up, you two.

00:04:28.059 --> 00:04:29.185
Huh?

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:42.699
[Aoi] We're all set to play.

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:45.535
I'll be watching your throws
to see what number you roll,

00:04:45.618 --> 00:04:47.453
then I'll remove the stones from the bowl.

00:04:48.037 --> 00:04:50.123
Can I inspect everything before we start?

00:04:50.206 --> 00:04:51.082
Of course.

00:04:53.876 --> 00:04:56.004
We haven't manipulated them in any way.

00:04:56.087 --> 00:04:58.089
Huh?

00:04:58.172 --> 00:04:59.090
Huh?

00:04:59.173 --> 00:05:01.467
Did Mary's friend just leave?

00:05:01.551 --> 00:05:03.970
She probably went
to the bathroom, or something.

00:05:06.055 --> 00:05:09.851
Anyways, we'll only be using the black
Go stones for this game, correct?

00:05:09.934 --> 00:05:12.395
-That's right.
-Okay, then.

00:05:12.478 --> 00:05:13.521
They look fine.

00:05:14.314 --> 00:05:16.190
I want to review them as well.

00:05:16.274 --> 00:05:18.985
What?
You're gonna start questioning me too?

00:05:19.068 --> 00:05:21.487
I'd expect nothing less from my fiancée.

00:05:21.571 --> 00:05:23.489
"Treat even a shallow river
like a deep one."

00:05:25.616 --> 00:05:27.702
I don't see an issue with these.

00:05:28.703 --> 00:05:30.121
Great. Who's gonna start?

00:05:30.955 --> 00:05:32.498
Saotome can go first.

00:05:33.124 --> 00:05:34.000
Cool.

00:05:34.083 --> 00:05:37.503
Right. Let the Dice Nim game commence.

00:05:37.587 --> 00:05:39.756
<i>My strategy is perfect</i>.

00:05:39.839 --> 00:05:41.841
<i>If I were only able to play by myself,</i>

00:05:41.924 --> 00:05:45.094
<i>I'd probably have a 50-50 chance</i>
<i>to win, at best.</i>

00:05:45.178 --> 00:05:46.512
<i>But with three of us,</i>

00:05:47.221 --> 00:05:50.016
<i>we are totally going</i>
<i>to dominate this game.</i>

00:05:53.102 --> 00:05:55.521
[Mary] <i>Hey. Listen up, you two.</i>

00:05:55.605 --> 00:05:58.524
Tsuzura, when I start
checking the equipment,

00:05:58.608 --> 00:05:59.776
I need you to leave.

00:05:59.859 --> 00:06:01.944
And make a bunch of noise
on your way out.

00:06:02.028 --> 00:06:03.654
Huh? Why?

00:06:03.738 --> 00:06:05.740
I don't have time to explain right now.

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:07.950
Just make
a lot of noise when you're leaving.

00:06:08.034 --> 00:06:10.370
When you're out,
I need you to go somewhere.

00:06:11.829 --> 00:06:14.999
<i>I can't say</i>
<i>I understand her reasons behind this,</i>

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:18.586
<i>but I know</i>
<i>I believe in Mary no matter what happens.</i>

00:06:18.669 --> 00:06:21.547
<i>If it's for her,</i>
<i>I would do anything for her.</i>

00:06:25.259 --> 00:06:26.427
It's two.

00:06:26.511 --> 00:06:29.555
Okay.
So that means I'm removing two stones.

00:06:32.266 --> 00:06:34.185
Next up is Sakura.

00:06:37.480 --> 00:06:38.314
Five.

00:06:38.398 --> 00:06:39.899
I'll take out five.

00:06:41.359 --> 00:06:42.318
<i>It'll be okay.</i>

00:06:42.902 --> 00:06:44.821
<i>Mary must have a plan.</i>

00:06:45.321 --> 00:06:48.825
<i>There's no way she would've taken the time</i>
<i>to prep us like that, if she didn't.</i>

00:06:50.243 --> 00:06:52.954
<i>But what if she ends up</i>
<i>being wrong about this?</i>

00:06:59.502 --> 00:07:02.964
<i>Calm down.</i>
<i>I can't keep overthinking things.</i>

00:07:03.047 --> 00:07:04.465
<i>I have to believe in her.</i>

00:07:08.094 --> 00:07:08.970
Three.

00:07:11.055 --> 00:07:13.891
Whoa. Doesn't look
like there's a lot of stones left.

00:07:13.975 --> 00:07:15.977
Mary, better not roll too high.

00:07:17.103 --> 00:07:18.980
-[Sakura] This is pathetic.
-[Mary gasping]

00:07:19.063 --> 00:07:20.648
I don't like this game.

00:07:20.731 --> 00:07:23.860
There's no technique or trick
that the players need to know to win.

00:07:23.943 --> 00:07:26.612
It's simpler than roulette,
but also much more boring.

00:07:26.696 --> 00:07:28.739
And if that weren't enough…

00:07:28.823 --> 00:07:29.866
Huh?

00:07:29.949 --> 00:07:31.617
The other one left?

00:07:31.701 --> 00:07:34.370
I wish they would do that
a little more quietly.

00:07:34.454 --> 00:07:36.622
Makes it easier to set up a distraction.

00:07:37.957 --> 00:07:40.042
[Sakura] Stop staring at me like that.

00:07:40.126 --> 00:07:41.377
Go! It's your turn.

00:07:42.086 --> 00:07:44.005
<i>Did I hear her right?</i>

00:07:44.088 --> 00:07:47.133
<i>Is she accusing me of trying</i>
<i>to distract them from something?</i>

00:07:47.717 --> 00:07:49.385
<i>Does she know my plan?</i>

00:07:49.469 --> 00:07:51.637
Soon there won't be stones left to pull.

00:07:52.138 --> 00:07:53.306
Go ahead and roll.

00:07:53.389 --> 00:07:54.765
Quick. End it.

00:07:54.849 --> 00:07:56.684
<i>No.</i>

00:07:56.767 --> 00:07:58.019
<i>It's gonna be all right.</i>

00:07:58.853 --> 00:08:01.105
<i>I'm positive I'll be able to win!</i>

00:08:08.613 --> 00:08:10.281
Looks like a six.

00:08:13.034 --> 00:08:13.868
One.

00:08:14.368 --> 00:08:17.038
<i>If I'm right,</i>
<i>there should only be seven stones left.</i>

00:08:17.121 --> 00:08:19.582
-Two.
-<i>Then it'll be her turn, and…</i>

00:08:19.665 --> 00:08:21.667
-Three.
-<i>…that'll be the end.</i>

00:08:21.751 --> 00:08:24.170
-Four.
-<i>I know there were six stones.</i>

00:08:24.253 --> 00:08:26.297
Five and six.

00:08:29.383 --> 00:08:30.801
Looks like we're done.

00:08:32.887 --> 00:08:35.014
You took the last stone that was left.

00:08:35.097 --> 00:08:37.183
No pieces remain for Sakura to take.

00:08:37.266 --> 00:08:39.560
-So, that means Mary loses.
-<i>What?</i>

00:08:41.062 --> 00:08:43.147
I don't… But how?

00:08:46.234 --> 00:08:48.236
[footsteps receding]

00:08:49.487 --> 00:08:50.696
Pardon my reach.

00:08:53.741 --> 00:08:56.035
-Wait. Stop! [gasping]
-[dice clattering]

00:08:56.661 --> 00:08:59.038
I see. Now I understand.

00:08:59.664 --> 00:09:00.540
You asked how?

00:09:02.124 --> 00:09:05.419
It must have been confusing for you
to lose, even after cheating.

00:09:05.503 --> 00:09:07.046
I saw through you.

00:09:09.715 --> 00:09:12.468
She was pocketing loaded dice
and switching them?

00:09:12.552 --> 00:09:13.844
That is correct.

00:09:13.928 --> 00:09:17.765
I'm confused. I thought Mibuomi
was the one who prepared the dice.

00:09:18.307 --> 00:09:21.519
Wouldn't it have been obvious
if something was off between each roll?

00:09:21.602 --> 00:09:24.855
He noticed what she did to the dice
and didn't say anything out loud.

00:09:24.939 --> 00:09:26.274
That's just who he is.

00:09:26.357 --> 00:09:28.859
Come on.
You're making me sound like a jerk.

00:09:28.943 --> 00:09:31.946
The rules didn't say anywhere
that players couldn't cheat.

00:09:32.029 --> 00:09:34.949
I think it's pretty impressive
if you can get away with it.

00:09:35.032 --> 00:09:36.951
It shows what someone can really do.

00:09:37.577 --> 00:09:38.744
Or it can.

00:09:38.828 --> 00:09:41.998
Doesn't mean much if you get caught
doing it before the game is over.

00:09:43.165 --> 00:09:44.292
Right, Mary?

00:09:46.294 --> 00:09:48.504
It was easy to spot your deception.

00:09:49.088 --> 00:09:51.674
<i>Your first attempt</i>
<i>was before the game even started.</i>

00:09:51.757 --> 00:09:54.260
<i>While the both of us</i>
<i>were examining the pieces,</i>

00:09:54.343 --> 00:09:56.512
<i>you put in one of your own dice</i>
<i>at that time.</i>

00:09:57.096 --> 00:10:00.975
<i>However, this initial die is not loaded</i>
<i>to favor any particular rolls,</i>

00:10:01.058 --> 00:10:04.645
so we were able to continue the game
without any noticeable issue.

00:10:05.730 --> 00:10:07.398
Now, as for the Go stones.

00:10:08.107 --> 00:10:09.859
The ones we requested for this challenge

00:10:09.942 --> 00:10:12.903
were delivered to this room
straight from the Go club.

00:10:12.987 --> 00:10:16.407
<i>Per the game's rules,</i>
<i>there are 181 black stones</i>

00:10:16.490 --> 00:10:19.410
<i>and 180 white stones.</i>

00:10:19.493 --> 00:10:22.538
<i>If a player knows how many pieces</i>
<i>there are in the bowl,</i>

00:10:22.622 --> 00:10:24.915
<i>it's easy to keep track</i>
<i>of how many remain.</i>

00:10:24.999 --> 00:10:28.252
We'll only be using the black Go stones
for this game, correct?

00:10:28.336 --> 00:10:32.423
<i>As we rolled, Saotome counted</i>
<i>the number of stones pulled.</i>

00:10:32.506 --> 00:10:36.927
<i>She bided her time, and waited until</i>
<i>there were seven stones left in play.</i>

00:10:38.179 --> 00:10:43.309
<i>Saotome saw her opportunity and switched</i>
<i>a weighted die with the one on the table.</i>

00:10:43.893 --> 00:10:46.437
This is the last game dice tossed.

00:10:46.520 --> 00:10:48.105
And this dice…

00:10:51.150 --> 00:10:52.443
only rolls a six.

00:10:53.319 --> 00:10:56.864
Which would have guaranteed
that I was left to take the final stone.

00:10:58.032 --> 00:10:59.659
She must have gone to great lengths

00:10:59.742 --> 00:11:01.869
to prepare as many loaded dice
as she could

00:11:01.952 --> 00:11:03.954
before playing against me today.

00:11:04.705 --> 00:11:08.459
But there was no way for us to know
what game we would be playing.

00:11:08.542 --> 00:11:11.379
Which means it wasn't possible
to use all of the dice

00:11:11.462 --> 00:11:13.214
she brought along in her pocket.

00:11:13.798 --> 00:11:16.842
That's the reason behind
swapping out the die more than once.

00:11:16.926 --> 00:11:20.680
As long as the dealer didn't notice,
there was still a chance she could win.

00:11:22.431 --> 00:11:25.726
<i>Additionally, she told her friends</i>
<i>to make loud noises when they were leaving</i>

00:11:25.810 --> 00:11:27.478
<i>so we'd be distracted.</i>

00:11:30.064 --> 00:11:34.402
I admit I admire your ability
to pivot in any given situation.

00:11:34.485 --> 00:11:37.738
Under normal circumstances,
there's no question I would have lost.

00:11:38.364 --> 00:11:39.532
What happened?

00:11:40.366 --> 00:11:42.618
How did I lose the game to you?

00:11:44.203 --> 00:11:46.747
I was supposed to be the winner. So, why?

00:11:48.582 --> 00:11:51.168
It's so simple
I didn't think I needed to explain.

00:11:51.252 --> 00:11:53.713
I pulled out one of the stones
before we started.

00:11:54.213 --> 00:11:55.506
It's not complicated.

00:11:57.591 --> 00:11:59.510
Your trick of swapping out dice

00:11:59.593 --> 00:12:01.387
was something
I was able to easily predict.

00:12:02.054 --> 00:12:05.141
I had a run-in with someone
that did the same thing the other day.

00:12:05.224 --> 00:12:08.018
It didn't work then,
and is not working now.

00:12:09.103 --> 00:12:10.187
If you're going to cheat,

00:12:10.271 --> 00:12:13.566
it's natural for me to assume
that you'd do anything to win.

00:12:14.859 --> 00:12:16.152
You set up the play,

00:12:17.361 --> 00:12:19.530
but I made you take the final stone.

00:12:19.613 --> 00:12:22.074
I'm capable
of skirting around the rules too.

00:12:23.117 --> 00:12:26.036
Today, you prepared
a well-thought-out deception.

00:12:26.120 --> 00:12:27.997
But just like Aoi said,

00:12:28.080 --> 00:12:30.207
it means nothing if you get caught.

00:12:30.708 --> 00:12:31.542
Saotome,

00:12:31.625 --> 00:12:35.087
you have proven that you're not worthy
to join Full-Bloom Council.

00:12:35.921 --> 00:12:37.548
You don't have what it takes.

00:12:46.390 --> 00:12:47.975
[Mary] <i>I can't believe it.</i>

00:12:48.058 --> 00:12:49.351
<i>I lost.</i>

00:12:49.894 --> 00:12:51.479
<i>My plan just went up in smoke.</i>

00:12:52.354 --> 00:12:55.107
<i>Nothing I did was enough</i>
<i>to beat this woman.</i>

00:12:58.110 --> 00:12:59.987
Okay. Let's make this official.

00:13:00.571 --> 00:13:03.991
Sakura Miharutaki is the winner
of our Dice Nim challenge.

00:13:04.617 --> 00:13:08.078
The treasure box she wagered
will be transferred from Mary to Sakura.

00:13:09.622 --> 00:13:12.875
<i>Mary Saotome,</i>
<i>was this all you had?</i>

00:13:14.084 --> 00:13:16.879
<i>I'm sure Aoi's thinking twice</i>
<i>about his obsession now.</i>

00:13:16.962 --> 00:13:20.299
No. Don't tell me
you're jealous of Mary Saotome?

00:13:20.382 --> 00:13:22.384
<i>Idiotic!</i>

00:13:24.386 --> 00:13:26.055
Very good, Sakura.

00:13:26.138 --> 00:13:28.557
I was surprised
to see such a well-fought battle

00:13:28.641 --> 00:13:30.810
from a game
I threw together so last-minute.

00:13:31.519 --> 00:13:32.728
Keep it to yourself.

00:13:32.812 --> 00:13:35.314
I don't get anything
out of being praised by you.

00:13:36.524 --> 00:13:37.566
Is that right?

00:13:37.650 --> 00:13:39.235
This is Miharutaki's.

00:13:39.318 --> 00:13:41.821
It's the treasure box Saotome wagered.

00:13:48.410 --> 00:13:50.830
[Mary] <i>I cheated, got caught, and lost</i>

00:13:50.913 --> 00:13:53.332
<i>after she took advantage</i>
<i>of what I was trying to do.</i>

00:13:54.917 --> 00:13:57.461
<i>I have no right to object to this.</i>

00:13:58.879 --> 00:13:59.839
[Mary] <i>That's fine.</i>

00:14:00.422 --> 00:14:03.843
<i>I'm still gambling. This isn't over yet.</i>

00:14:03.926 --> 00:14:06.720
Uh, I don't understand.

00:14:09.890 --> 00:14:12.226
[Sakura] This is the map
Saotome was given.

00:14:12.309 --> 00:14:16.021
Why is this placed
inside my treasure chest?

00:14:16.105 --> 00:14:17.731
Mary!

00:14:21.694 --> 00:14:22.736
Yes! You're back!

00:14:23.529 --> 00:14:24.530
Found it!

00:14:25.614 --> 00:14:26.532
[Mikura] Huh?

00:14:26.615 --> 00:14:29.201
They were right where you told us
they'd be, Mary.

00:14:29.285 --> 00:14:33.330
<i>What? There was another</i>
<i>treasure box we're supposed to find?</i>

00:14:33.414 --> 00:14:34.999
<i>What are they doing with that? </i>

00:14:35.082 --> 00:14:36.500
<i>What is going on here?</i>

00:14:37.626 --> 00:14:40.296
What's wrong?
You're messing with me, right?

00:14:40.379 --> 00:14:42.548
Oh. You look pale.

00:14:43.048 --> 00:14:45.801
You know, you don't have to tell me,
but if I were to guess,

00:14:46.552 --> 00:14:49.305
you haven't figured out
what's going on yet?

00:14:50.681 --> 00:14:53.642
[Mary] I guess a Council member
isn't that big of a threat.

00:14:54.643 --> 00:14:56.854
Mind explaining for the rest of us?

00:14:56.937 --> 00:14:59.315
What's with the new treasure boxes
your friends brought in?

00:15:00.065 --> 00:15:01.233
I'd be happy to.

00:15:01.317 --> 00:15:03.694
We were operating
from a false understanding of the game

00:15:03.777 --> 00:15:04.945
right from the start.

00:15:05.654 --> 00:15:08.532
<i>We solved the puzzle of the map</i>
<i>using the clues we found.</i>

00:15:08.616 --> 00:15:11.952
<i>And understanding the map</i>
<i>led us to the first of the treasure boxes.</i>

00:15:12.036 --> 00:15:14.914
<i>We thought we could access</i>
<i>the treasure inside them</i>

00:15:14.997 --> 00:15:17.291
<i>by using the key</i>
<i>on the other player's lock.</i>

00:15:18.042 --> 00:15:20.586
But all of that was based
off an assumption.

00:15:21.295 --> 00:15:22.546
Maybe I'm wrong,

00:15:22.630 --> 00:15:25.966
but when you were looking at your map,
you assumed it was for this building.

00:15:26.050 --> 00:15:27.927
That's what we were told off the bat.

00:15:28.010 --> 00:15:30.220
Which of the floors did you search first?

00:15:30.304 --> 00:15:33.140
First floor. Where else would I start?

00:15:33.223 --> 00:15:35.267
We did the same thing ourselves.

00:15:35.351 --> 00:15:38.604
We searched the first floor
and found those titles from kid songs.

00:15:39.939 --> 00:15:43.317
However, the setting
for this entrance exam,

00:15:43.400 --> 00:15:44.818
the student club building,

00:15:44.902 --> 00:15:46.737
is actually four-stories tall.

00:15:47.321 --> 00:15:50.240
And there are two numbered musical
notations that are slightly different.

00:15:50.824 --> 00:15:53.369
So, how do we interpret this information?

00:15:53.953 --> 00:15:55.871
This was the conclusion I came to.

00:15:57.164 --> 00:16:00.125
<i>The two numbered musical notations</i>
<i>represent a point on the map</i>

00:16:00.209 --> 00:16:02.378
<i>that has three-dimensional coordinates.</i>

00:16:03.462 --> 00:16:06.465
That was the real secret
we needed to decode.

00:16:06.548 --> 00:16:07.383
Just look.

00:16:08.467 --> 00:16:10.844
My lovely assistant
found this treasure chest

00:16:10.928 --> 00:16:13.555
in the room located
at the three-dimensional coordinates.

00:16:13.639 --> 00:16:15.641
This is what we were really looking for.

00:16:18.727 --> 00:16:20.771
But still, with the numbered notations

00:16:20.854 --> 00:16:24.149
there was no way to know
which axis was vertical or horizontal.

00:16:24.233 --> 00:16:26.652
<i>That's why I had the two of them split up.</i>

00:16:26.735 --> 00:16:29.655
<i>Having them leave the room wasn't just</i>
<i>a trick to distract you</i>

00:16:29.738 --> 00:16:31.740
<i>from what I was trying to do at the table.</i>

00:16:32.241 --> 00:16:34.284
That's pretty clever of you.

00:16:35.494 --> 00:16:37.162
I'm impressed, Mary.

00:16:37.246 --> 00:16:40.165
Congratulations. You are correct.

00:16:41.500 --> 00:16:45.379
So while we played,
that was all a ploy to buy time.

00:16:45.462 --> 00:16:47.631
No. I don't think I'd say that.

00:16:48.132 --> 00:16:51.343
My understanding of the coordinates
would only get us one chest.

00:16:51.844 --> 00:16:54.930
And maybe I was a bit too overeager
to win at this point,

00:16:55.014 --> 00:16:56.932
but I couldn't give up on the possibility

00:16:57.016 --> 00:16:59.685
that our treasure boxes
really had the answers.

00:17:00.394 --> 00:17:03.689
That's when I decided I was going
to get all the treasure chests.

00:17:04.481 --> 00:17:05.691
When did you know?

00:17:06.734 --> 00:17:09.945
It was right after the three of us
figured out how to solve the first riddle.

00:17:10.612 --> 00:17:12.698
<i>When I saw you there waiting</i>
<i>before we even finished,</i>

00:17:12.781 --> 00:17:15.701
<i>I gotta be honest,</i>
<i>I didn't know what to do.</i>

00:17:16.285 --> 00:17:18.746
Was there any chance
I could win against you?

00:17:18.829 --> 00:17:20.748
I couldn't help worrying about it.

00:17:21.373 --> 00:17:24.251
Your confidence was enough
to leave me feeling shaken.

00:17:24.960 --> 00:17:28.255
<i>But it was ultimately</i>
<i>what led to you showing me your map.</i>

00:17:29.339 --> 00:17:30.841
You knew you would win.

00:17:30.924 --> 00:17:33.010
You advertised your biggest weakness,

00:17:33.093 --> 00:17:34.428
and we exploited it.

00:17:35.012 --> 00:17:37.181
You lost because you underestimated us!

00:17:37.264 --> 00:17:38.766
That pride was your downfall.

00:17:40.350 --> 00:17:41.518
Am I wrong?

00:17:41.602 --> 00:17:44.313
You were the one that said it was okay
for my friends to help.

00:17:44.396 --> 00:17:45.856
Oh, man. That was good.

00:17:45.939 --> 00:17:48.275
Ooh, you really thought
you were playing on easy mode.

00:17:48.358 --> 00:17:50.527
-Mary!
-Let me have this!

00:17:50.611 --> 00:17:52.279
She thought
she was so much better than us.

00:17:52.362 --> 00:17:54.031
She's a loser! Loser!

00:17:54.114 --> 00:17:56.533
-Big, old idiot loser!
-Yeah. You're right.

00:17:56.617 --> 00:17:57.493
Huh?

00:17:58.077 --> 00:18:00.037
I've been very condescending to you

00:18:00.996 --> 00:18:04.291
My arrogance allowed me
to be caught off-guard, and I lost.

00:18:04.833 --> 00:18:05.793
I was wrong.

00:18:07.628 --> 00:18:10.047
I think you're extraordinarily talented.

00:18:11.131 --> 00:18:13.050
I apologize for my rudeness.

00:18:13.634 --> 00:18:16.553
<i>Whoa.</i>
<i>She's so much more mature than I am.</i>

00:18:20.099 --> 00:18:22.184
-[both] Huh?
-What the hell is this?

00:18:24.353 --> 00:18:26.563
That would be the prize
you were all trying to track down.

00:18:26.647 --> 00:18:28.315
Uh…

00:18:28.398 --> 00:18:30.275
The game is now over.

00:18:30.359 --> 00:18:32.820
Mary Saotome is today's winner.

00:18:32.903 --> 00:18:34.196
-Heck yes!
-We won!

00:18:34.738 --> 00:18:37.324
I can't believe how far ahead you were.
That's so amazing!

00:18:37.407 --> 00:18:41.078
Well, sure. But it's only because
of you two that I won.

00:18:41.703 --> 00:18:42.913
Thank you.

00:18:48.418 --> 00:18:51.880
[Mikura] <i>Who do you think you are,</i>
<i>Sakura Miharutaki?</i>

00:18:51.964 --> 00:18:53.590
<i>How dare you lose?</i>

00:18:53.674 --> 00:18:55.926
<i>My plan was perfect.</i>

00:18:56.009 --> 00:18:59.346
<i>But now everything is falling apart</i>
<i>because of you!</i>

00:18:59.429 --> 00:19:01.974
-What do I do with this?
-<i>Saotome has a collar now.</i>

00:19:02.683 --> 00:19:03.976
<i>This isn't over.</i>

00:19:04.059 --> 00:19:06.979
<i>I'll take that collar from her,</i>
<i>whatever it takes! </i>

00:19:07.062 --> 00:19:11.066
<i>I'm the only one</i>
<i>who deserves Mistress Juraku's discipline!</i>

00:19:11.150 --> 00:19:12.484
<i>Only me!</i>

00:19:13.068 --> 00:19:17.447
Now, then. The wager was for you
to gain entry privileges into Full-Bloom.

00:19:17.990 --> 00:19:21.952
Mary shall have unlimited right of entry
whenever she's ready to join.

00:19:22.578 --> 00:19:24.872
Any objections, Aoi? Now's the time.

00:19:25.455 --> 00:19:26.748
No. None from me.

00:19:26.832 --> 00:19:29.835
So I have time to choose
if I wanna join. Good to know.

00:19:30.878 --> 00:19:34.006
[Aoi] I gotta say. You are every bit
the woman I thought you were!

00:19:34.089 --> 00:19:35.841
With you, we can do it!

00:19:35.924 --> 00:19:38.552
Come on, Mary.
Why don't you join Full-Bloom!

00:19:38.635 --> 00:19:40.888
Hang on.
You just said I could take my time.

00:19:40.971 --> 00:19:43.891
It'd be a waste for us
to let someone so talented get away!

00:19:43.974 --> 00:19:45.767
-Uh…
-I'm begging you, Mary!

00:19:45.851 --> 00:19:48.145
-Think of it as helping a friend out!
-Too close!

00:19:48.228 --> 00:19:51.398
I'm asking too, Saotome. Please join us.

00:19:51.481 --> 00:19:54.526
You are more than qualified
to serve on the council for the club.

00:19:54.610 --> 00:19:56.612
Thanks. I appreciate the enthusiasm.

00:19:56.695 --> 00:19:58.864
Hey, hey.
What's going on here, Sakura?

00:19:58.947 --> 00:19:59.781
Huh?

00:19:59.865 --> 00:20:02.159
Why do you think your opinion is relevant?

00:20:02.242 --> 00:20:03.202
What?

00:20:03.285 --> 00:20:06.413
Well, because I'm serving
as a Council member too.

00:20:06.997 --> 00:20:10.250
Why would you think that?
After all this, you're definitely fired.

00:20:11.543 --> 00:20:12.628
Huh?

00:20:13.712 --> 00:20:15.047
You wouldn't!

00:20:15.130 --> 00:20:17.341
You let me go from losing one time?

00:20:17.424 --> 00:20:20.761
After everything I've done to prove
that I'm capable before this happened?

00:20:20.844 --> 00:20:23.013
This time is the problem, though.

00:20:23.096 --> 00:20:24.932
You have the track record,

00:20:25.015 --> 00:20:26.350
you could have easily won,

00:20:26.934 --> 00:20:29.061
but you couldn't follow through
when it mattered.

00:20:29.144 --> 00:20:31.146
Fate's abandoned you this time around.

00:20:31.647 --> 00:20:33.774
We can't keep you as a member of the club.

00:20:33.857 --> 00:20:36.526
You'll just end up being a liability
to everyone if we do.

00:20:37.236 --> 00:20:39.488
We don't need people who fall behind.

00:20:41.114 --> 00:20:42.866
You can stand there scared.

00:20:42.950 --> 00:20:44.701
Lean on the rest of us to save you.

00:20:44.785 --> 00:20:46.745
Keep being a damsel in distress.

00:20:46.828 --> 00:20:49.414
Be pitiful for the rest of your time here.

00:20:51.500 --> 00:20:53.210
No way. Really?

00:20:53.293 --> 00:20:56.296
Wait. You were thinking
about joining up with the Full-Bloom club?

00:20:56.380 --> 00:20:58.006
Oh. Of course, I was.

00:20:58.090 --> 00:21:01.218
You're worth 100 members.
I'm excited to have you.

00:21:01.301 --> 00:21:04.012
I'm a lucky guy. My fiancée's amazing.

00:21:05.597 --> 00:21:07.015
<i>So what now?</i>

00:21:07.099 --> 00:21:09.518
What does this mean for the two of us?

00:21:09.601 --> 00:21:11.520
Are you going to call off our wedding?

00:21:11.603 --> 00:21:12.604
Huh?

00:21:13.480 --> 00:21:15.732
You're disappointed
in me, right?

00:21:16.233 --> 00:21:19.528
You can't marry someone
who'd just keep causing problems.

00:21:20.946 --> 00:21:23.865
That's stupid!
I'd never do something like that.

00:21:24.533 --> 00:21:28.704
There are benefits that come with powerful
families getting married I want.

00:21:28.787 --> 00:21:31.039
Couldn't care less
about what kind of human you are.

00:21:31.123 --> 00:21:32.708
It doesn't matter to me.

00:21:36.336 --> 00:21:38.422
You… What?

00:21:38.505 --> 00:21:40.173
What? Are you surprised?

00:21:40.257 --> 00:21:41.925
Now I'm the one you're underestimating.

00:21:43.010 --> 00:21:45.470
You're right. I see your point.

00:21:46.555 --> 00:21:50.434
If the Mibuomi
and Miharutaki families are joined,

00:21:50.517 --> 00:21:53.020
we would be
one of the most powerful in Japan.

00:21:54.062 --> 00:21:57.190
That would be stupid to call it all off.

00:22:00.027 --> 00:22:02.654
Well, back to what actually matters.

00:22:02.738 --> 00:22:05.949
I know I'm kinda sounding like
a broken record today, but hear me out.

00:22:06.825 --> 00:22:09.036
I really want you in Full-Bloom.

00:22:11.288 --> 00:22:13.165
I promise you won't regret it.

00:22:13.248 --> 00:22:15.459
And I'll do whatever it takes
to make it worth your while.

00:22:16.626 --> 00:22:18.962
EPISODE SIX: A RESISTING GIRL

00:22:20.547 --> 00:22:21.465
Huh?

00:22:22.549 --> 00:22:23.967
-[Mikura gasping]
-[Sachiko cackling]

00:22:29.848 --> 00:22:32.726
Could you please
take your hands away from me?

00:22:32.809 --> 00:22:33.977
Hmm?

00:22:34.061 --> 00:22:36.480
Why would I ever wanna be tied
to a stupid group

00:22:36.563 --> 00:22:38.357
headed by a fricking idiot?

00:22:38.440 --> 00:22:40.484
I will never join Full-Bloom!

00:22:40.567 --> 00:22:43.362
No matter what! I will never!

00:22:48.909 --> 00:22:50.243
[Tsuzura] <i>And that was it.</i>

00:22:50.327 --> 00:22:52.496
<i>Mary's plan to way</i>
<i>to pick a winning horse</i>

00:22:52.579 --> 00:22:54.539
<i>between the Full-Bloom club</i>
<i>and Student Council</i>

00:22:54.623 --> 00:22:57.542
<i>wrapped up much sooner</i>
<i>than any of us could have imagined.</i>

00:23:03.715 --> 00:23:05.675
<i>I think that's part of Mary's style.</i>

00:23:10.430 --> 00:23:14.059
[Tsuzura] <i>Togakushi is probably worried</i>
<i>about what might happen to us.</i>

00:23:16.019 --> 00:23:19.147
<i>But, to be honest,</i>
<i>I'm just really happy we did it.</i>

00:23:20.107 --> 00:23:22.025
GAMBLING DEN REOPENING
NEW GAME DOUBT POKER

00:23:22.692 --> 00:23:25.278
<i>And while we may not have</i>
<i>some grand plan to do it,</i>

00:23:25.862 --> 00:23:29.449
<i>I still think the three of us</i>
<i>are going to find our own way of winning.</i>

00:23:32.869 --> 00:23:34.788
[Tsuzura] <i>Whenever I see a smile</i>
<i>on Mary's face, </i>

00:23:35.455 --> 00:23:38.291
<i>I know part of that wish for me</i>
<i>has already come true.</i>

00:23:45.757 --> 00:23:47.384
There's no way to really know

00:23:47.467 --> 00:23:50.387
what kind of challenges
might be waiting for us down the road,

00:23:50.887 --> 00:23:55.267
<i>but whatever might happen,</i>
<i>I know I'll be with Mary.</i>

00:23:55.892 --> 00:23:57.853
<i>She's everything.</i>

00:23:57.936 --> 00:23:59.146
<i>Walking into my life</i>

00:23:59.229 --> 00:24:02.816
<i>and extending a hand to save me</i>
<i>without asking a thing in return.</i>

00:24:04.401 --> 00:24:06.069
<i>Mary is my prince!</i>

00:24:10.907 --> 00:24:12.909
[ending theme music playing]

00:25:41.790 --> 00:25:44.960
So you think you'll give up on Saotome
now that she's turned you down?

00:25:45.043 --> 00:25:46.962
Absolutely not.

00:25:47.045 --> 00:25:48.797
I'm totally obsessed with her.

00:25:48.880 --> 00:25:52.050
I can tell she's gonna end up being
a big player at this school.

00:25:52.133 --> 00:25:53.009
Oh.

00:25:53.093 --> 00:25:56.388
I can't believe you can still say that
after you got burned.

00:25:56.471 --> 00:25:57.931
See? That's the thing.

00:25:58.014 --> 00:26:02.269
I really need her to join Full-Bloom
regardless of what she might want.

00:26:02.769 --> 00:26:04.020
Otherwise…

00:26:06.064 --> 00:26:07.941
I'm gonna have to crush her.
